  "body": "### Summary of Changes\n\nThe 3D Pocket roughing ladder now applies `stock_to_leave` in both radial and axial directions.\n\n- **Level target query:** In `crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs`, query `level_target(facets, footprint, z - axial_leave)` instead of plane `z`. This keeps tool radius plus stock allowance XY distance from material overhead, so top faces and shallow slopes keep their allowance.\n- **Flat floor detection:** In `crates/motion/src/machining3d/floor_levels.rs`, when `stock_to_leave > 0.0`, search for horizontal upward faces across `[bottom_z, top_z)` and deduplicate levels within `1e-9` mm. This ensures deep floors receive a level at `floor + stock_to_leave`.\n- **Catalog case update:** Regenerated catalog case `3d/rough-finish` using `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish`.\n- **Decision document:** Added `docs/decisions/3669-3d-pocket-stock-to-leave.md`.\n\n### Readings and Verification\n\n- Passed all 4 integration tests in `crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_stock_to_leave.rs`:\n  - `through_pocket_without_floor_cuts_to_bottom_z_and_keeps_wall_allowance`\n  - `flat_top_boss_and_floor_both_keep_axial_allowance`\n  - `rough_finish_dome_and_plate_keep_axial_and_radial_allowance`\n  - `dome_allowance_holds_across_strategies_shell_and_rest`\n- `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rough-finish` completed cleanly.\n\n### What Was Not Exercised\n\n- Multi-axis rotary continuous toolpaths (`pocket3d_air_split` preserves existing behavior with `axial_leave = 0.0`).\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket roughing now keeps the stock allowance axially on tops, shallow slopes, and floors as well as radially.\n\nFixes #3669\nRefs #2392\n",
